{"questions":[{"question_id":"1lfz0omn6","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2008 Paper 2 Offline","year":2008,"examDate":2008,"subject":"chemistry","chapter":"solid-state","chapterGroup":"physical-chemistry","topic":"close-packing-in-crystals","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"pthe-number-of-atoms-in-this-hcp-unit-cell-isp-jee-advanced-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-jkkzlhdn2cmxpqpk","content":"<p>The number of atoms in this HCP unit cell is :</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"4"},{"identifier":"B","content":"6"},{"identifier":"C","content":"12"},{"identifier":"D","content":"17"}],"correct_options":["B"],"explanation":"<p>The number of atoms in a HCP unit cells is 6.</p>\n<p>3 atoms are at the middle of the unit cell and each atom contributes 1 atom to the unit cell.</p>\n<p>2 atoms are at the two face centres of the unit cell and each atom contributes 1/2 atom to the unit cell.</p>\n<p>12 atoms are at the 12 corners of the unit cell and each atom contributes 1/6 atom to the unit cell.</p>\n<p>The number of atoms in one unit cell</p>\n<p>(3 <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0.02ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.09ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -491 778 482\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"D7\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-D7\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> 1) + (2 <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0.02ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.09ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -491 778 482\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"D7\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-D7\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> 1/2) + (12 <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0.02ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.09ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -491 778 482\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"D7\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-D7\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> 1/6) = 3 + 1 + 2 = 6</p>"}]}